@startuml
title GotIt operational administration - owner authorization and audited command
actor Staff
participant "Admin browser" as UI
participant "Admin gateway" as Gateway
participant "Core API" as Core
participant "GotIt API (product command)" as Product
database "Core schema" as CoreDB
database "Product schema" as ProductDB

Staff -> UI: Sign in with Google/password
UI -> Gateway: Allowlisted authentication exchange
Gateway -> Core: Authenticate, then GET /auth/me
Core --> Gateway: Active verified application admin
Gateway --> UI: Validated session

Staff -> UI: Unlock editing with authenticator code
UI -> Gateway: POST /admin-api/security/verify
Gateway -> Core: POST /api/v1/admin/mfa/verify
Core -> CoreDB: Check encrypted credential, lockout and unused TOTP step
Core --> UI: Session-bound five-minute step-up (via gateway)

Staff -> UI: Save explicit target, revision and audit reason
UI -> Gateway: Command + operation UUID + bearer + step-up
Gateway -> Core: Validate trusted identity
Gateway -> Product: GET /admin/access
Product -> Core: Verify application/actor, permission and step-up
Core -> CoreDB: Load current role, permissions, MFA revision
Core --> Product: Trusted capabilities
Product --> Gateway: Curated capabilities
Gateway -> Product: Allowlisted command
Product -> Core: Independently reauthorize command
Core --> Product: Authorization result
alt authorized
  Product -> ProductDB: BEGIN, operation lock, compare receipt fingerprint
  alt matching receipt exists
    ProductDB --> Product: Replay original persisted result
  else new command and expected revision matches
    Product -> ProductDB: Scoped domain write + audit event + receipt, COMMIT
    ProductDB --> Product: Persisted result
  else stale revision or changed payload
    Product -> ProductDB: ROLLBACK
    Product --> Gateway: 409 conflict
  end
  Product --> Gateway: Bounded result
  Gateway --> UI: Persisted/replayed result or safe conflict
else unauthorized or MFA expired
  Product --> Gateway: 403, no domain write
  Gateway --> UI: Safe rejection; retain form
end
note over Core,CoreDB
Core-owned identity/access commands use their own
transaction, audit and receipt in Core's schema.
No distributed cross-service transaction is claimed.
end note

Staff -> UI: Change another user's role/permissions or Free/Pro access
UI -> Gateway: Explicit staff/plan action + revision + reason + UUID
Gateway -> Core: Check current identity and action-specific capability
Core -> CoreDB: staff.write or billing.write + session-bound MFA
Gateway -> Core: POST /admin/users/:id/staff or /plan
Core -> CoreDB: BEGIN; serialize staff action before actor locks
Core -> CoreDB: Reauthorize actor; compare receipt and user revision
alt staff action
  Core -> CoreDB: Reject self changes and unverified promotion
  Core -> CoreDB: Replace role/permissions; revoke sessions; bump MFA revision
else access action
  Core -> CoreDB: Set/clear scoped plan override with optional expiry
  note right of CoreDB
  Paddle subscriptions, charges and prepaid
  minute sources remain unchanged.
  end note
end
Core -> CoreDB: Audit + receipt + user revision; COMMIT
Core --> Gateway: Persisted/replayed result
Gateway --> UI: Refresh effective role/plan from Core billing resolver
@enduml
